  <iati-identifier>GB-GOV-1-400124-407</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safeguarding the Genuineness of Public Votes of the 2024 Elections Through Crowd-Sourced Election Results Recapitulation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In regards to implementation of the 2024 elections, there is a deep concern from political observers, politicians, and presidential candidates that there is a potential electoral fraud. Some are worried that the state institutions and their apparatus will not be neutral in the election. There is a big concern that there are some attempts to mobilize state apparatus to support certain political parties and/or candidates. In addition, people are also worried about the independence of electoral management body, especially KPU, in conducting the 2024 elections. Several electoral observers and activists considered KPU not transparent and not independent in conducting the electoral stages. And therefore, NEGRIT initiates a project in which NETGRIT and its coalition will organize public participatory monitoring during vote counting and results recapitulation process in the 2024 election in Indonesia. This program is called crowd-sourced election results.</narrative>
  </description>
